@startuml
hide empty description
[*] --> FAST_DISABLED
FAST_DISABLED --> FAST_READY : mode=shadow|active AND prerequisites valid
FAST_READY --> FULL_IDLE_CONFIRM : FULL_IDLE candidate
FULL_IDLE_CONFIRM --> FULL_IDLE : confirm elapsed on distinct samples
FULL_IDLE_CONFIRM --> RESERVE_UNKNOWN : candidate lost
FAST_READY --> NEAR_LIMIT : NEAR_LIMIT candidate
FAST_READY --> RESERVE_UNKNOWN : neither proven branch
FULL_IDLE --> RESERVE_UNKNOWN : export/branch disappears
NEAR_LIMIT --> RESERVE_UNKNOWN : reserve no longer proven
RESERVE_UNKNOWN --> FULL_IDLE_CONFIRM : FULL_IDLE candidate
RESERVE_UNKNOWN --> NEAR_LIMIT : NEAR_LIMIT candidate

state FAST_DISABLED
state FAST_READY
state FULL_IDLE_CONFIRM
state FULL_IDLE
state NEAR_LIMIT
state RESERVE_UNKNOWN

note right of FULL_IDLE
Desired overlay O = export
O attacks toward target at A400 W/s
end note
note right of NEAR_LIMIT
reserve = primary_max - primary_actual
Desired O = max(0, export - reserve)
A400 attack / R100 release
end note
note right of RESERVE_UNKNOWN
O = 0 immediately for unproven reserve.
Controlled release exists only for a
previously proven FULL_IDLE/NEAR_LIMIT episode.
end note
note bottom of FAST_READY
Global force-zero/block examples:
mode=off, grid import, stale/invalid data,
MAX_SOC, command path not ready,
missing power limits, Cross-Charge correction,
manual/night/discharge/safe-state.

shadow: calculate diagnostics, command stays B
active: physical target may become B+O
end note
@enduml
